      "body": "## Overview\n\nWith `--allowed-local-media-path` set, a `file://` URL inside the allowed directory that points to a missing file (or to a directory) fails the request with a 500. The path comes straight from the request, so it should be a client error like the \"must be a subpath\" check right above it. Noticed while reading `MediaConnector._load_file_url`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- An `image_url` / `video_url` / `audio_url` with a `file://` URL to a nonexistent file or a directory raises `ValueError` (HTTP 400) instead of `FileNotFoundError` / `IsADirectoryError` (HTTP 500).\n- Existing files load as before.\n\n## Validation\n\n```python\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom vllm.entrypoints.serve.exception_handling.error_response import create_error_response\nfrom vllm.multimodal.media import MediaConnector\n\nwith tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as d:\n    connector = MediaConnector(allowed_local_media_path=d)\n    try:\n        connector.fetch_video((Path(d) / \"missing.mp4\").as_uri())\n    except Exception as e:\n        err = create_error_response(e).error\n        print(type(e).__name__, err.code, err.type)\n```\n\n```text\n# main (03091e28b)\nFileNotFoundError 500 InternalServerError\n# this PR\nValueError 400 BadRequestError\n```\n\nSame for `fetch_image`, and for a directory. I added `test_fetch_image_local_files_not_a_file` (sync and async, missing file and directory); both cases fail on main.\n\n```\npytest tests/multimodal/media/test_connector.py\nruff check && ruff format --check   # on the two touched files\n```\n\nBoth pass locally on CPU. I didn't start a server, so the 400 is checked through `create_error_response` rather than over HTTP.\n\n## Details\n\nIt's one `is_file()` check after the subpath check in `_load_file_url`, which both the sync and async paths go through. I used a plain `ValueError` to match the neighbouring subpath error. A remote URL that 404s is already reported as a client error since #47165; this is the local-file counterpart.\n\nNot a duplicate as far as I can tell: I didn't find an issue or PR for missing local files. The open PRs that touch `connector.py` are about redirects and SSRF (#55539, #59716, #57825, #43897), the media cache (#56062, #55616) and decode metrics (#49682, #50875); none of them adds an existence check.\n\nAI assistance was used to find and prepare this change.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
